Z||000000||LemonSky||01-09-2001||07:06 PM||||Out of curiosity, I recently went to the Kelly Blue Book site to see what the value of my 1986 Gold SE6 is. Several months ago, when I checked, the value was $2360. But today it's $2405, a whooping $45 increase! Since mine has increased in value, then everyone else's probably has also (although the likelihood of getting the KBB price is very low, or so I've been told).||||reg||11
Z||000001||FieroLisa||01-09-2001||09:34 PM||||Good call! As of today my coupe is worth $2,095 and the GT is worth $4,090!!!!!!(Ha like I could sell it for that but that's just OK)<BR>Last time I checked the coupe it was at like $1,200 or maybe $1,500 tops and the GT was worth $3,495 in September. Interesting...<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR>*As Always, Updated Website*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||01-09-2001||09:37 PM||||Like most car prices, it really depends on the person buying it.  Im sure that if someone tried to sell their car here, they could get more for it just because likely the person that is buying it could really appreciate it.  I believe my Fiero is worth about $1300, by the KBB, but mostly because of the high miles (220,000)   If it werent for those miles, I bet I could get much more.  I've even found people's buisness cards stuck in my window, saying that if I ever wanted to sell, call them....<P>As if I would ever sell my baby!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by FieroJoe (edited 01-09-2001).]||||reg||1
